* ddcutil user-defined feature file -- Samsung Odyssey G95NC (Neo G9 57", Dual UHD 7680x2160)
*
* Vendor VCP codes for PBP / PIP / 3PBP control, reverse-engineered from the
* Windows "Samsung Display Manager" DDC/CI traffic (DXVA2 SetVCPFeature) and
* validated by direct replay against the monitor.
*
* TODO before use: set MODEL and PRODUCT_CODE from your own `ddcutil detect`
* output (EDID). MFG_ID is SAM. Values below were captured on Windows; please
* confirm read/write behavior with native ddcutil on Linux.

MFG_ID       SAM
MODEL        <fill from `ddcutil detect`>
PRODUCT_CODE <fill from `ddcutil detect`>
MCCS_VERSION 2.1

FEATURE_CODE E2 PBP/PIP Mode and Layout
  ATTRS NC RW
  VALUE x00 Off (exit PBP/PIP to single source)
  VALUE x01 PBP on, 2-way (last-used split)
  VALUE x02 PBP 2-way, large-left / small-right
  VALUE x03 PBP 2-way, 50/50
  VALUE x04 PBP 2-way, large-left (~21:9 left pane)
  VALUE x05 PBP 2-way, uneven split
  VALUE x06 3PBP, narrow/square center with larger sides
  VALUE x07 3PBP, 50/25/25 (large-left)
  VALUE x08 3PBP, 25/50/25 (large-middle)
  VALUE x09 3PBP, 25/25/50 (large-right)
  VALUE x10 PIP
* NOTE: `getvcp E2` reads back a STATUS value of the form 0x39NN, NOT the command
* value above. Observed: cmd 0x07->0x3909, 0x08->0x390b, 0x09->0x390d (status low
* byte = 2*cmd - 5); 2-way-on->0x3901, PIP->0x390f. Use the command values with
* `setvcp`. A 3PBP layout write briefly drops DDC while the monitor re-enumerates.

FEATURE_CODE E3 PBP/PIP Pane Source
  ATTRS NC RW
* 16-bit value = (channel << 8) | source_code
*   channel:     0x00 left/main, 0x01 middle, 0x02 right
*   source_code: 0x00 HDMI1, 0x01 HDMI2, 0x02 HDMI3, 0x10 DisplayPort
* examples:
*   ddcutil setvcp E3 0x0110   middle pane -> DisplayPort
*   ddcutil setvcp E3 0x0201   right pane  -> HDMI2
* `getvcp E3` returns a packed status (high byte 0xc0 in 3PBP, 0x10 in 2-way).

FEATURE_CODE E8 PBP/PIP Sound Source
  ATTRS NC RW
* max value 0x02 (three options); 0x00 observed as default.

FEATURE_CODE 60 Input Source
  ATTRS NC RW
  VALUE x0f DisplayPort
  VALUE x11 HDMI-1
  VALUE x12 HDMI-2
* HDMI-3 and value x32 (decimal 50) seen in capability data but not yet confirmed.
